[{"id":"fm-core1-1.05-q1","number":1,"question":"<p>Find an equation of the form</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{f}(z)=z^2+pz+q\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are complex numbers, given each of the following pairs of roots:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z=1+i\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z=3+2i\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z=-3+4i\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z=1+5i\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z=-2+2i\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z=2-2i\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}&amp;(z-(1+i))(z-(3+2i))\\\\&amp;=z^2-(3+2i)z-(1+i)z+(1+i)(3+2i)\\\\&amp;=z^2-(4+3i)z+1+5i\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}&amp;(z-(-3+4i))(z-(1+5i))\\\\&amp;=z^2-(1+5i)z-(-3+4i)z+(-3+4i)(1+5i)\\\\&amp;=z^2+(2-9i)z-23-11i\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}&amp;(z-(-2+2i))(z-(2-2i))\\\\&amp;=z^2-(2-2i)z-(-2+2i)z+(-2+2i)(2-2i)\\\\&amp;=z^2+8i\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.05-q2","number":2,"question":"<p>Find an equation of the form</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{f}(z)=z^3+pz^2+qz+r\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are complex numbers, given that the solutions to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{f}(z)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z=1+i\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z=-1+i\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z=2+2i\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}&amp;(z-(1+i))(z-(-1+i))(z-(2+2i))\\\\&amp;=(z^2-2iz-2)(z-(2+2i))\\\\&amp;=z^3-(2+4i)z^2-(6-4i)z+(4+4i)\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.05-q3","number":3,"question":"<p>A polynomial is defined by</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{f}(z)=z^3-(5+6i)z^2+(35+27i)z-58-30i\" data-display=\"true\"></span><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1+9i)^3\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Hence show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z=1+9i\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a solution to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{f}(z)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol><p>It is known that a second solution to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{f}(z)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"3\"><li><p>Find the remaining solution, writing your answer in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a+bi\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are integers to be found.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}(1+9i)^3&amp;=(1+9i)(1+9i)(1+9i)\\\\&amp;=(1+9i)(-80+18i)\\\\&amp;=-80-720i+18i-162\\\\&amp;=-242-702i\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}&amp;(1+9i)^3-(5+6i)(1+9i)^2+(35+27i)(1+9i)-58-30i\\\\&amp;=-242-702i-(5+6i)(-80+18i)-208+342i-58-30i\\\\&amp;=-242-702i+508+390i-266+312i\\\\&amp;=0\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore z=1+9i\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a solution.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}(z-2)(z-(1+9i))&amp;=z^2-(1+9i)z-2z+(2+18i)\\\\&amp;=z^2-(3+9i)z+(2+18i)\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So for some complex number <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(z^2-(3+9i)z+(2+18i))(z-k)=k^3-(5+6i)k^2+(35+27i)k-58-30i\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Comparing constants:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"-(2+18i)k=-58-30i\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"k=\\frac{58+30i}{2+18i}\\times\\frac{2-18i}{2-18i}=\\frac{656-984i}{328}=2-3i\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><strong>Alternative Method:</strong></p>","<p>Sum of roots: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5+6i=(1+9i)+(2)+(a+bi)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow a=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b=-3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2-3i\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.05-q4","number":4,"question":"<p>Given that</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{f}(z)=z^2-(2+3i)z-k\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a complex number and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1+2i\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a root of the equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{f}(z)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1-2i\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is not a root of the equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{f}(z)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}(1+2i)^2-(2+3i)(1+2i)-k&amp;=0\\\\-3+4i+4-7i-k&amp;=0\\\\\\therefore k&amp;=1-3i\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}&amp;(1-2i)^2-(2+3i)(1-2i)-(1-3i)\\\\&amp;=-3-4i-8+i-1+3i\\\\&amp;=-12\\ne0\\text{ so not a root.}\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.05-q5","number":5,"question":"<p>It is known that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2-i\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a root of</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{f}(z)=z^3-3iz^2+2z+k\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a complex number</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2+i\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is not a solution to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{f}(z)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>All the coefficients are not real, so must use factor theorem.</p>","<p>Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2-i\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a root, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{f}(2-i)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}(2-i)^3-3i(2-i)^2+2(2-i)+k&amp;=0\\\\&amp;=(2-i)(5-4i)-3i(5-4i)+4-2i+k=0\\\\&amp;=2-11i-12-9i+4-2i+k=0\\\\&amp;=-6-22i+k=0\\\\\\therefore k&amp;=6+22i\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}&amp;(2+i)^3-3i(2+i)^2+2(2+i)+6+22i\\\\&amp;=(2+i)(3+4i)-3i(3+4i)+4+2i+6+22i\\\\&amp;=2+11i+12-9i+4+2i+6+22i\\\\&amp;=24+26i\\ne0\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore\" data-display=\"false\"></span> by the factor theorem <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2+i\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is not a factor and so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2+i\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is not a root of the equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{f}(z)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.05-q6","number":6,"question":"<ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{f}(z)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> such that</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"z^3-i=(z+i)\\mathrm{f}(z)\" data-display=\"true\"></span></li><li><p>Hence find all the solutions to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z^3-i=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}z^3-i&amp;=(z+i)(z^2-iz-1)\\\\\\mathrm{f}(z)&amp;=z^2-iz-1\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(z+i)(z^2-iz-1)=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Consider the quadratic factor:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"z=\\frac{i\\pm\\sqrt{(-i)^2+4}}2=\\frac{i\\pm\\sqrt3}2=\\pm\\frac{\\sqrt3}2+\\frac12i\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So the solutions are <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z=i\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z=\\frac{\\sqrt3}2+\\frac12i\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z=-\\frac{\\sqrt3}2+\\frac12i\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.05-q7","number":7,"question":"<p>Find the solutions to</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"z^2-(8-5i)z+3-29i=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"z=\\frac{8-5i\\pm\\sqrt{(8-5i)^2-4(3-29i)}}2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Consider just the discriminant:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(8-5i)^2-4(-15i)=39-80i-12+116i=27+36i\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So now find</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{27+36i}=a+bi\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for real numbers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"27+36i=(a+bi)^2=a^2-b^2+2abi\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Solve</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a^2-b^2=27\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"36=2ab\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>simultaneously:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}b&amp;=\\frac{18}a\\text{ so }a^2-\\left(\\frac{18}a\\right)^2=27\\\\a^4-324&amp;=27a^2\\\\a^4-27a^2-324&amp;=0\\\\(a^2-36)(a^2+9)&amp;=0\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is real, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a^2=36\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=6\" data-display=\"false\"></span> or <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=-6\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>So that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> or <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b=-3\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>That is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{27+36i}=6+3i\" data-display=\"false\"></span> or <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-6-3i\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"z=\\frac{8-5i\\pm(6+3i)}2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"z=\\frac{14}2-\\frac22i\\text{ or }z=\\frac22-\\frac82i\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z=7-i\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z=1-4i\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.05-q8","number":8,"question":"<p><strong>The following questions should be solved by using methods relating the coefficients of a polynomial to sums and products of its roots</strong></p><p>Given</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"z^2-(10-2i)z+k=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a complex number has roots <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"6-2i\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","steps":["<p>Sum of roots: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a+6-2i=10-2i\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=4\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Product of roots: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4(6-2i)=24-8i\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore k=24-8i\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.05-q9","number":9,"question":"<p>Given</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"z^2-kz=-6-21i\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a complex number has roots <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2+7i\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","steps":["<p>Sum of roots: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a+2+7i=k\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Product of roots: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a(2+7i)=6+21i\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"a=\\frac{6+21i}{2+7i}=\\frac{3(2+7i)}{2+7i}=3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3+2+7i=k\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore k=5+7i\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.05-q10","number":10,"question":"<p>It is given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1+i\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and 3 are solutions of</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"z^3-2iz^2+pz+q=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are complex numbers. Determine the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","steps":["<p>Since the coefficients are not real, there are no complex conjugate roots.</p>","<p>Sums of roots: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1+i+3+a=2i\\ \\therefore a=-4+i\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Sums of pairs of roots: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p=3(1+i)+(-4+i)(1+i)+3(-4+i)=-14+3i\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Product of roots: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q=-3(1+i)(-4+i)=15+9i\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore p=-14+3i\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q=15+9i\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.05-q11","number":11,"question":"<p>It is given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2+i\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-4\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are solutions of</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"z^3+pz^2-(5+8i)z-q=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a complex number and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a real positive number. Find the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","steps":["<p>Since the coefficients are not real, there are no complex conjugate roots.</p>","<p>Let <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> be the remaining root</p>","<p>Sums of pairs of roots: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-4(2+i)+a(2+i)-4a=-5-8i\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}-8-4i+2a+ai-4a&amp;=-5-8i\\\\a(-2+i)&amp;=3-4i\\\\a&amp;=\\frac{3-4i}{-2+i}\\times\\frac{-2-i}{-2-i}=\\frac{-10-5i}5=-2+i\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Sum of roots: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p=-(-4+(2+i)+(-2+i))=4-2i\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Product of roots: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q=-4(2+i)(-2+i)=(-8-4i)(-2+i)=20\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore p=4-2i\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q=20\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.05-q12","number":12,"question":"<p>It is given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2-3i\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and 3 are solutions of</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"2z^3+pz^2+qz-13=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are complex numbers. Determine the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","steps":["<p>Since the coefficients are not real, there are no complex conjugate roots.</p>","<p>Let <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> be the remaining root</p>","<p>Product of roots: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{13}2=3(2-3i)a\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}13&amp;=(12-18i)a\\\\a&amp;=\\frac{13}{12-18i}\\times\\frac{12+18i}{12+18i}=\\frac{156+234i}{468}=\\frac13+\\frac12i\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Sum of roots: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac p2=-\\left(3+(2-3i)+\\left(\\frac13+\\frac12i\\right)\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac p2=-\\left(\\frac{32}6-\\frac{15}6i\\right)\\Rightarrow p=-\\frac{32}3+5i\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Sums of pairs of roots: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac q2=3(2-3i)+\\left(\\frac13+\\frac12i\\right)(2-3i)+3\\left(\\frac13+\\frac12i\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}\\frac q2&amp;=6-9i+\\frac{13}6+1+\\frac32i\\\\\\frac q2&amp;=\\frac{55}6-\\frac{15}2i\\Rightarrow q=\\frac{55}3-15i\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore p=-\\frac{32}3+5i\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q=\\frac{55}3-15i\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.05-q13","number":13,"question":"<p>The equation</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"z^3-(10-2i)z^2+pz+q=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are complex numbers has solutions <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z=a\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z=b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z=a+bi\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for real values <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Find the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Sum of roots: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"10-2i=a+b+a+bi\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Considering imaginary part: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-2=b\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Considering real part: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"10=2a+b\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore a=6\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b=-2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Sums of pairs of roots: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p=-2(6)-2(6-2i)+6(6-2i)=12-8i\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Product of roots: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-q=-2(6)(6-2i)=-72+24i\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore p=12-8i\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q=72-24i\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.05-q14","number":14,"question":"<p><strong>Prerequisite knowledge for Q14: Argand Diagrams</strong></p><p>The solutions of</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"z^3-(6+3i)z^2+(9+14i)-15i=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>all lie on the same straight line in the complex plane. It is known that two of the solutions are <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z=1+2i\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><p>Find the remaining solution, writing your answer in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a+bi\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are integers to be found.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}6+3i&amp;=3+(1+2i)+\\alpha\\\\6+3i&amp;=4+2i+\\alpha\\\\\\therefore&amp;\\ 2+i\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]}]